# Wave W17-O (Route 115): swim post — a swimmer’s marker post at the falls’ foot pool: a post with a white board head carrying a blue wave line, standing on the shore verge where the swimmer’s morning round begins (design: the swimmer swims this shore and salutes the falls every morning). On mist turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Ragged Pass’s spring post by the wave board: that post marks spring water on a stair; this one marks a swimming shore.
